      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T21:13:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this isn\u0027t ideal since the behavior change is silent and non-obvious. But it\u0027s provided as a fallback for an uncommon but valid case. The rustc \"-l\" flags inability to deal with libraries that don\u0027t start with \"lib\" was why we moved away from this in the first place, see https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/1410907. I worry that throwing a warning here would just cause build noise from any valid use cases.",
      "parentUuid": "22e839d7_40c2ed84",
      "revId": "45ad91c2c90a816431e8a6be08a5c3f7d1818ce9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
